  "type": "MULTIPLE_CHOICE",
  "data": {
    "body": "Let $T: \\mathbb{R}^{n} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}^{m}$ be a linear transformation and $T(\\mathbf{x})=A \\mathbf{x}$, where $A$ is the standard matrix for $T$. Which of the following statements must be TRUE?\n\n(i) $A$ is an $n \\times m$ matrix.\n\n(ii) If the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, then $T$ is one-to-one.\n\n(iii) If $m>n$, then $T$ is onto.\n\n(iv) If $n>m$, then $T$ is one-to-one.\n\n(v) If the columns of $A$ span $\\mathbb{R}^{m}$, then $T$ is onto.",
    "solution": [
      2
    ],
